-- title:
--   Localised modular ring of level Nq gives a valuation dichotomy
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$ with $q \nmid N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$. Work inside the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((\mathfrak q))$ and consider two subobjects of it: the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the images, under the coefficientwise embedding of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$, of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull (N * q)` (itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the divisor expansions of level $Nq$); and the subring $\mathcal{O} =$ `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (N * q) A.toSubring red`, namely the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two level-$Nq$ expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` at the kernel of coefficientwise reduction along $\mathrm{red}$: explicitly, the set of Laurent series $f$ for which $f s = r$ with $r, s$ in that subring and $s$ not reducing to $0$. The assertion is that for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)`, either the Laurent series underlying $g$ lies in $\mathcal{O}$, or the Laurent series underlying the inverse $g^{-1}$ formed in that field lies in $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   The dichotomy says that the intersection of the localised modular ring of level $Nq$ with the function field of $X_0(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a valuation ring of that field, reflecting the regularity of the standard model of $X_0(Nq)$ at the generic points of its special fibre at $q$ in the range $q \nmid N$. It is used in the construction of prolongation tuples and of models compatible with the cusp and order laws at places specialising to characteristic $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_coe_mem_modularLocalized_or_coe_inv_mem_modularLocalized_mul_of_not_dvd.lean

